{"title":"AMC 10 2021 (Mock) Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_2021_(Mock)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e5875e7c5442adfbe66652956da8ea84601935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B - C = 2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65fe88ab68f524a33cd3b600a84148d8f61971c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B + C - A = 2021$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/c/5ec9bb43944c2285f00f23c316e7cbca8352cc3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + C - B = 2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd10f8367ee571add2f701789e465fa23d91c8ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B + C - 2020 - 2021 - 2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"265\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e2dd5ea574c64f00d21c3f17fdb9a80c3a327e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 0\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 2020\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 2021\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 2022\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 6063$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"453\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_2021_(Mock)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bag of marbles consists of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red marbles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blue marbles. Each of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> marbles are pulled out one at a time. What is the probability that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84a16aa6c1b1e8185c9279f12332fdeded9bd00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5th$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> marble pulled out is red?\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c50fa6f00d2b319291088267d00681a83ae0c29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\frac{1}{5}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\frac{3}{7}\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\frac{4}{7}\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"364\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_2021_(Mock)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Meena has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> snakes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are purple and the rest are green. Some of the snakes are poisonous. She knows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the poisonous snakes are green and the number of poisonous snakes which are purple is double the amount of poisonous snakes that are green. How many snakes are not poisonous?\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b19070d7d46ce2cb32e18a22921f1a23b79fd898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 3 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 4 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 5\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }6\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ }7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"344\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_2021_(Mock)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At a birthday celebration consisting of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> kids, each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> kids purchase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> soda cans except for the birthday kid, who purchases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4e80582d50572c4ea84dc35d4cfa14e79f67957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2S$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> soda cans. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> soda cans cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> quarters. How many dollars were spent total on the soda cans?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bb9345a1cd05b6f53fad6f35e0d4cf2303dd906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\frac{(K - 1)Q}{6}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\frac{(K - 1)Q}{4}\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\frac{KQ}{4}\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\frac{(K + 1)Q}{4}\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{(K + 1)Q}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"656\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_2021_(Mock)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a quadratic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e269c3da583870f7ad6b27df6ff1e2ea9be8ef73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Ax^2 + Bx + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are nonzero, have two distinct, real roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0dbfa28bcb1b0f91a6cab22d10ac26c25818e33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40ef7a5d44e2884c6fcba4721db9147f7165b055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, which of the following conditions must be true?\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9f801f3b6b29434a7e166a03776481b13f19fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } B^2 - 4A = 0 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } B - 24A \\ge 0 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } B^3 - A^2 \\ge 24 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } A + B = 6 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } B + 24A - C = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"841\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_2021_(Mock)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two glass containers stand on a tabletop. The first one is a solution consisting of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb7e03ccc8985ba9d029ea4add6e3e15ab9a953a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> water and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> alcohol. The second solution consists of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af59f5a81354c1925a58cb897e1d142111b1d7c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> water and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/1/ff169c8eb4e8e515216bcd0f6f207a78af94c8b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> alcohol. A third container is placed on the same table and must be a mixture of the first and second solutions in a particular ratio. After the third container is filled as per these conditions, it consists of an equal amount of alcohol and water. What is the ratio of the amount of the first solution mixed in the third container and the amount of the second solution mixed in the third container?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/9559b36c83bb911a6fac255c85d241b7eba34e74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 1 : 4\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 1 : 3 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 1 : 2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 2 : 1 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 3 : 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"466\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_2021_(Mock)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/292f1d68563503adaac690c46f899be87b9cc536.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 3 - 5 + 7 + 9 - 11 + … + 475 + 477 - 479$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"371\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b630d62dd42a46333db0e3f1d9212adb76aa8e85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 16,340 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 17,280 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 18,220 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 19,160 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 20,100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"567\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_2021_(Mock)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> be a segment in the real coordinate plane. How many points C exist on the same plane, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles?\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018072016\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 224/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8218/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22311:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018072016 and revision id 293764. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}